        "node_id": "n_9_2afea2",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of using a Binary Indexed Tree (BIT) which requires maintaining a separate array for the prefix sums, we can use a Segment Tree to efficiently handle both the updates and queries. Segment Trees support both point updates and range queries in logarithmic time, making them suitable for this problem. Additionally, since the values of \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are relatively small, we can precompute the values for each position in the range to avoid recalculating them repeatedly during updates. This approach ensures that our solution remains efficient even for large inputs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2520455546156282057",
